{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "description": "Registry of PDB HETATM component IDs known to be crystallization additives, buffer components, phasing agents, detergents, and other non-ligand entities commonly encountered in macromolecular crystal structures. Entries with remove_by_default=true are automatically removed by the structure-preparator curation stage unless the profile explicitly overrides via keep_additives.",
  "last_updated": "2026-09-15",
  "notes": [
    "Comp_ids are 1–3 uppercase characters as used in PDB HETATM records.",
    "CCD type is from the _chem_comp.type field in the RCSB Chemical Component Dictionary.",
    "A comp_id listed here with remove_by_default=true does not automatically make every occurrence an additive; the heuristic complement (Section 7 of the design plan) must also be applied.",
    "This registry is a superset of the interaction-profiler SKIP_LIGAND and COFACTORS sets. Entries in the COFACTORS category here are NOT auto-removed by default because they may be the ligand of interest.",
    "Entries verified against: PDB CCD, RCSB stats, published surveys (Rupp 2009, Chayen 2004, McPherson 2009)."
  ],
